From 9de6a4a8dd2497fef1fd05f3338e32544a833623 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vraxa <200693817+vraxa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:30:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Replay Plus 1.3.1: exported frames sized by the game's own
 video frame

- an exported frame's size is the game's video frame's, as the render side sees it go to be copied out for the
  encoder (B8G8R8A8, not a swap chain buffer, RENDER_TARGET -> COPY_SOURCE each frame), checked against the export's
  own H.264 setup when it had one (an MP4: one run after the export before ended); the buffer the frame came in is
  only a bound
- 1.3 sized each frame by the buffer it came in, but the game reads its frames back into six buffers in turn and not
  every one is a buffer of its own: a 1280x720 WebM had one buffer at the start of a block of three frames, finished
  as one tall picture and written over the two after it (three frames in six broken), and an MP4 had every sixth
  frame go out without the lens once its H.264 setup was four seconds old
- a frame whose size cannot be told for sure goes out as the game made it, and the log says which and why
